x86_64-linux  clang emits only the C2 variant of an *inline* constructor on this target and cxx1 emits C1 and C2 - the difference base-implicit-constructor-emitted.nonames records. Every constructor here is written inside its class: a class template's cannot be moved out of line, and a constructor template never can. The other two targets compare every name and agree, which is what proves the constructor-template mangling (C1/C2 with the arguments and the pattern parameters, and the Microsoft ??$?0 form).
